{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nGenerated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST\nbe omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit\nworkspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate. The unit tests are in `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]`, and the CLI tests are in `tests/authoring_cli.rs`. I did not read any implementation source. The obligations of `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` map to tests as follows.\n\n- **Combining contributions and including every applicable one.**\n  - `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` checks, for a requirement subject, that the declaration, cited requirements one hop away, an example that references the subject, terms (including a term cited by another term), and `{test}` nodes are all present.\n  - The same test checks that unrelated items (an `{impl}` item, the parent `impl[Thing]` node, a distant requirement) and earlier evidence inputs are absent.\n  - `only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs` covers the cite, impl and test edge directions, including example subjects and a parent subject.\n  - `references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes` covers markdown sections and plain-text files.\n  - `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` and `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` cover `:impl:` and `:test:` anchors.\n  - `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` and `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` cover citation and site subjects.\n- **Deduplicating identical selections.**\n  - `citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once` asserts exact counts of 1 for a requirement cited twice, a term shared by two requirements, and a built-in cited twice. It also asserts a total of 5.\n  - `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` anchors the same file with both `:impl:` and `:test:`. It asserts that the whole input list equals exactly the declaration plus one file entry.\n  - The CLI test `implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read` asserts that a node is recorded once.\n- **Reporting unresolvable inputs before inference.**\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request]` disallows the subject's own declaration. It asserts a nonzero exit status, a stderr message naming the path, no connection to the model endpoint, and unchanged evidence.\n  - `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation`, `unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference` (missing file, missing node, disallowed path) and `mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort` cover denied and unreadable inputs at preparation.\n  - `mandatory_git_inputs_require_staging_declarations_sources_and_terms` covers untracked declarations and terms, with the `git add` hint.\n  - `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` shows that stale recorded inputs are not treated as mandatory.\n- **The complete set is supplied in the initial request.**\n  - `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` checks the serialized first prompt for the mandatory item hash, the requirement text and the built-in text.\n  - `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` checks the prompt for the anchored node's text and the absence of sibling text.\n  - `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` checks that the first HTTP request contains the requirement, the definition and the test source.\n- **Generated `evidence/` output.**\n  - `generated_evidence_anchors_are_omitted_unless_allowed_and_abort_when_disallowed` checks all four cases. The default exclusion omits the file (the input count stays 1). A symlink alias into `evidence/` is also omitted. An explicit allow includes the file. An explicit disallow aborts with `PermissionDenied` and names the path.\n  - `generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default` checks reference discovery under `evidence/`.\n- **Obligation on contributing requirements to cite this one and define their sources.** This is a documentation obligation on other requirements, not harness behavior. Those requirements carry it out themselves, so it needs no test here.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "5e119b23ee95abcacb9104190da269b67b7e85e7e3a806f9a712233a1e425674",
